                <pb facs="0417" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/3098: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-01T18:00:00-04:00">August 1, 1941—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>616. Your 957, July 29, 9 p.m. Should you be approached in connection with the
                    possibility of Murphy visiting Vichy, you may reply that you have been informed
                    by the Department that the present status of the arrangement as regards North
                    Africa will necessitate his continued presence there for the time being. It is
                    felt that he will be needed there to continue to supervise the operation of this
                    agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
